-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Ikari Warriors
  Publisher   Elite Systems, 1988
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Ikari Warriors (1988)(Elite Systems)(48K-128K).z80
  MD5         54ad66af6678df22a9d4443e3d04aadb

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Players get bare skin with a red headband for player 1 and a
              blue one for player 2; enemies wear steel-blue uniforms with
              skin faces, so players stand out at a glance. The scenery takes
              the arcade's colours: dark olive ground, green foliage, blue
              water, wooden bridges, grey rocks and bunkers. A painted set,
              colourist not named.

  Changes     1.1: the game keeps its own CPU speed after each sprite update
              instead of being set back to 3.5 MHz, the screen copy at 14 MHz
              or faster; works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next 26.11). 1.2: the
              game now holds the original's pace: quiet scenes were faster
              than the original and busy scenes slower; sprite images already
              seen are kept in memory and no longer worked out again. 1.3:
              Enhanced gains scenery in the arcade's colours: the ground,
              foliage, water, wooden bridges, rocks and bunkers are coloured
              pixel by pixel on the tilemap, under the game's own black ink;
              the colour now scrolls with the scenery. The default is
              unchanged.

  Note        No outline on the figures, in both default and Enhanced: the
              owner chose that for this game. Known issues: the game reads a
              few ROM bytes as data and gets the Next ROM's values, not the
              48K ROM's (effect on play not established); pace in JNext
              against the original, 6 runs of 600 updates: default overall
              -0.62 to +0.64%, busy +1.81% at most; Enhanced overall -0.27 to
              +0.91%, quiet -1.81 to -0.14%, busy +0.05 to +2.13%; stretches
              of 20 updates up to +15.7% default and +18.2% Enhanced where new
              images are first drawn; in Enhanced, attract, hi-scores and GAME
              OVER keep the original scenery colours, and the yellow paper of
              the two gun icons shows black. Missing: no AY music, as this
              snapshot is the game's 48K form; the cheats are the archive's
              and have not been played; not yet checked: a level end, driving
              a tank, scenery past the part traced (it takes each char's usual
              colour); hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite fuel
   3  Infinite ammo
   4  Infinite grenades
